    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Cal Raleigh** leading our charge at a 78.97 efficiency score. **Cal Raleigh** is our primary target for production, buoyed significantly by a high-leverage park factor (+14%) and a favorable matchup against Sugano (xERA 4.91). While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.07) and **Bryce Harper** (64.58) provide elite floors, **JJ Bleday** (63.38) stands out as an aggressive start today; his 14% platoon edge against Peterson makes him a high-efficiency play despite the moderate park profile. We are leaning heavily into these veteran anchors to capitalize on matchups against mediocre rotations, effectively offsetting the lower-tier projections elsewhere in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the morning was holding **Zack Gelof** at a 39.57 efficiency score, keeping him just below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" While **Zack Gelof** carries an intriguing profile, the combination of facing an elite arm in Williams (xERA 2.91) and a significant defensive penalty from the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time (1.86s) squeezed his upside, pushing him to the bench in favor of safer, high-volume contributors. Similarly, **Jung Hoo Lee** fell just short (38.51) due to a lingering platoon disadvantage against Dreyer. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the volatile matchup for **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Dylan Beavers**, both of whom are tasked with navigating Misiorowski (xERA 2.32). While the park factor provides a +16% boost to their profiles, the underlying SP Skill penalty (-19%) against such a dominant arm introduces real variance. We are effectively betting on their speed and lineup order to compensate for the quality of the opposing starter, as the scarcity of stolen bases dictates that even riskier bats like **Dylan Beavers** must remain in the lineup if we hope to close the gap in the category standings.",
